  "enhanced_information": "Chemotherapy primarily targets rapidly dividing cells, which explains the varying susceptibility of different cell types. Cardiac myocytes are terminally differentiated and do not divide, making them highly resistant to chemotherapy. In contrast, enterocytes and hematopoietic cells have high turnover rates and are therefore more susceptible to chemotherapeutic agents. Hair follicle cells also divide rapidly and are susceptible to chemotherapy. Liver hepatocytes possess regenerative capacity, but they can still be affected by certain chemotherapeutic agents. Thus, the most resistant cell type to chemotherapy is cardiac myocytes."
